To install a mod, first locate your Battlezone: Combat Commander installation directory and open the "addon" folder.
If the folder doesn’t exist, you can create one yourself.
Extract the contents of the mod you downloaded into its own subfolder inside the "addon" folder.
For example, if the mod is called "MyCoolMod", it should go into a folder like "...\addon\MyCoolMod".
Then, launch the game, go to the Options menu, select Addon Mods, and check the box next to the mod you want to use.
Restart the game if the game asks you to.